{"step_index":2776,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-22T12:53:51Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-22T15:53:51+03:00\nCompleted At: 2026-09-22T15:53:51+03:00\nFile Path: `file:///d:/AI_Engineer/Pharmacy-agy/desktop_app/templates/index.html`\nTotal Lines: 2487\nTotal Bytes: 96098\nShowing lines 1990 to 2045\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n1990: async function submitProcess() {\n1991:     const t = I18N[currentLang] || I18N.ar;\n1992:     if (selectedShortageFiles.length === 0 || selectedWarehouseFiles.length === 0) {\n1993:         showToast(t.select_at_least_one, 'error');\n1994:         return;\n1995:     }\n1996:     \n1997:     const btn = document.getElementById('btn-submit');\n1998:     const progressModal = document.getElementById('progress-modal');\n1999:     \n2000:     // UI Loading state\n2001:     btn.classList.add('hidden');\n2002:     progressModal.style.display = 'flex';\n2003:     document.getElementById('progress-text').innerText = t.progress_init;\n2004:     document.getElementById('progress-bar-fill').style.width = '5%';\n2005:     startProgressTimer();\n2006:     \n2007:     const termEl = document.getElementById('pipeline-log-terminal');\n2008:     if (termEl) termEl.innerHTML = '[System] Started pipeline...\\n';\n2009:     \n2010:     try {\n2011:         const res = await window.pywebview.api.start_process(\n2012:             JSON.stringify(selectedShortageFiles), \n2013:             JSON.stringify(selectedWarehouseFiles)\n2014:         );\n2015:         if (res.success) {\n2016:             currentProcessId = res.process_id;\n2017:             \n2018:             // If the backend detected an identical exact match that was already completed!\n2019:             if (res.existing) {\n2020:                 showToast(t.process_existing, 'info');\n2021:                 // Simulate process_complete event\n2022:                 setTimeout(() => {\n2023:                     window.dispatchEvent(new CustomEvent('process_complete', {\n2024:                         detail: {\n2025:                             process_id: res.process_id,\n2026:                             success: true,\n2027:                             stats: res.stats\n2028:                         }\n2029:                     }));\n2030:                 }, 500);\n2031:             } else {\n2032:                 // Background process started\n2033:                 showToast(t.toast_started, 'success');\n2034:             }\n2035:         } else {\n2036:             showToast((currentLang === 'en' ? 'Error: ' : 'خطأ: ') + res.error, 'error');\n2037:             btn.classList.remove('hidden');\n2038:             progressModal.style.display = 'none';\n2039:             stopProgressTimer();\n2040:         }\n2041:     } catch (error) {\n2042:         showToast(currentLang === 'en' ? 'Connection error' : 'حدث خطأ أثناء الاتصال', 'error');\n2043:         btn.classList.remove('hidden');\n2044:         progressModal.style.display = 'none';\n2045:         stopProgressTimer();\nThe above content does NOT show the entire file contents. If you need to view any lines of the file which were not shown to complete your task, call this tool again to view those lines.\n"}
{"step_index":2777,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-22T12:53:51Z","thinking":"The `submitProcess()` function uses a global flag, `isProcessRunning`, to prevent duplicate process submissions; this flag is set to true on success and false on error or completion. The design appears to prevent users from accidentally initiating multiple processes concurrently. It is necessary to understand whether switching screens during a running process should be permitted, as it is unclear if the running process blocks screen switching.\n\n\nThe full-screen progress modal blocks access to the \"system logs\" link; this must be addressed. A button within the modal will allow viewing the logs and hiding the modal, permitting access to the terminal while the process runs. Ensuring the \"new process\" button is disabled during process execution prevents accidental submissions.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"replace_file_content","args":{"AllowMultiple":false,"Description":"Update progress-modal CSS to fixed global overlay","EndLine":452,"Instruction":"Update #progress-modal CSS to position: fixed and high z-index","ReplacementContent":"#progress-modal {\n    position: fixed; \n    top: 0; left: 0; right: 0; bottom: 0;\n    width: 100vw; height: 100vh; \n    background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.7); \n    z-index: 99999; \n    align-items: center; \n    justify-content: center;\n    backdrop-filter: blur(6px);\n    display: none;\n}\n#progress-modal .progress-box {\n    background: white; \n    padding: 30px; \n    border-radius: 14px; \n    max-width: 520px; \n    width: 90%; \n    box-shadow: 0 25px 50px -12px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.35); \n    text-align: center;\n}","StartLine":433,"TargetContent":"#progress-modal {\n    position: absolute; \n    top: 0; left: 0; right: 0; bottom: 0;\n    width: 100%; height: 100%; \n    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.85); \n    z-index: 9998; \n    align-items: center; \n    justify-content: center;\n    backdrop-f